  "race": "half_elf",
  "class": "rogue",
  "spellcastingAbility": "cha",
  "background": "sage",
  "backstory": "They never spoke their name within the hallowed, dust-choked halls of the Great Archive, for they believed that to name a thing is to limit its potential. Born of a restless union between a human scholar and an elven exile, they spent their formative years not in the sun, but beneath the flickering glow of enchanted candles, devouring scrolls that others feared to touch. While their peers studied history to learn from the past, this silent seeker studied it to find the keys to the future. They frequently boasted of having read every volume within the world’s greatest repositories, a claim punctuated by a cold, calculating gaze that suggested they had not just read the words, but had dissected the very souls of the authors who wrote them.\n\nThe transition from scholar to rogue was not a loss of discipline, but a practical refinement of it. They realized early on that the most potent secrets are kept behind iron grates, complex locks, and lethal traps. To master the world, one must first master the art of treading where one is not invited. They trade in the currency of shadows, using a blade not for simple malice, but with the surgical precision of an anatomist. While others recoil in terror at the sight of a rift-born horror, they are the one standing in the fray, ink-stained fingers dancing across parchment as they record the rhythmic pulsing of a demon’s secondary heart. To them, every monster is a lesson, and every drop of ichor is a vital footnote in their growing magnum opus.\n\nThis lifelong obsession has culminated in a series of leather-bound tomes—a definitive codex on the forbidden lore of the planes—which they carry with the reverence of a holy relic. This work is not merely a collection of facts, but a roadmap to ultimate dominion. They adventure not for gold or the hollow praise of heroes, but for the missing chapters that can only be found in the blood-stained ruins and darkest corners of the earth. They believe that once the final word is written and the last anatomical secret is bared, the laws of reality will bow to their whim. Knowledge is the only true path to power, and they will pick every lock and slit every throat necessary to claim the throne that hidden truth provides.",
  "alignment": "chaotic_evil",
  "name": "ljn",
